      "reasons": [
        "The provided packet describes misspecification in statistical general linear models for crossover clinical trial analysis, not something in the field of cognition.",
        "The definition’s general framing (“use of a statistical model that is set up incorrectly… leaving out or wrongly defining important effects…”) is only exemplified in the packet specifically as misspecified period effects, carryover effects, and variance-covariance structures in GLMs; the packet does not support broader/general claims about misspecification beyond these examples.",
        "“Including higher false-positive rates or reduced power” is supported by the packet as inflated type I error and declined power, but the overall field assignment to cognition is unsupported."
